                        <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>

                        <p>
                            These Terms &amp; Conditions form an agreement between you and Brandora.
                            They apply when you create an account, browse the platform, or use any
                            part of the service.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            By registering an account or continuing to use Brandora, you confirm
                            that you have read these terms, that you accept them, and that you have
                            the authority to do so &mdash; including on behalf of a company, if you
                            are signing up as a brand. If you do not accept these terms, please do
                            not use the platform.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            These terms should be read together with our
                            <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>, which explains how we
                            handle information about you.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <!-- 2 -->

                    <article class="tc-card" id="about-brandora">

                        <h2>2. About Brandora</h2>

                        <p>
                            Brandora is an influencer marketing platform. It gives brands a place to
                            publish campaigns and find creators, gives influencers a place to present
                            their work and receive offers, and provides the tools both sides use to
                            agree deliverables, submit work for approval, and move money in tracked
                            milestones.
                        </p>

                        <div class="tc-note">
                            <p>
                                <strong>What Brandora is:</strong> the platform on which brands and
                                influencers find one another and run the mechanics of a
                                collaboration, together with the payment facility that holds
                                milestone funds until work is approved.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                <strong>What Brandora is not:</strong> a party to the commercial
                                agreement between a brand and an influencer. The deliverables,
                                schedule, and price of a collaboration are agreed between those two
                                parties. Brandora is not an employer, an advertising agency, or a
                                guarantor of either side's performance.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <p>
                            Brandora does administer the payment and dispute mechanisms described in
                            sections 8 and 12, and holds milestone funds until a milestone is
                            approved or a dispute is resolved. That administrative role does not make
                            Brandora responsible for the underlying agreement.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <!-- 3 -->

                    @* ASSUMPTION: the codebase does not enforce or record a minimum age
