                    <article class="tc-card" id="payments">

                        <h2>8. Payments, Fees and Wallets</h2>

                        <h3>How milestone payments work</h3>
                        <p>
                            Milestone payments are made through the platform using the supported
                            mobile financial service providers. Funds for a milestone are held once
                            paid and are released to the influencer's earnings when the milestone is
                            approved. A payment is only treated as successful once it has been
                            verified directly with the payment provider &mdash; returning to the site
                            after a checkout does not by itself confirm that a payment succeeded.
                        </p>

                        <h3>Platform fees</h3>
                        <p>
                            Brandora charges a platform fee on collaborations. The fee applies on both
                            sides: a brand pays the fee in addition to the milestone amount, and a fee
                            is applied to an influencer's earnings when they are withdrawn. The rate
                            in effect is shown to you before you confirm a payment or a withdrawal.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            The fee rate that applies to a given payment is fixed at the time that
                            payment is released, so a later change to our rates does not alter
                            earnings you have already accrued. We may change our fee rates for future
                            transactions.
                        </p>

                        <h3>Earnings and withdrawals</h3>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Approved milestone payments are credited to the influencer's earnings balance on the platform.</li>
                            <li>Influencers nominate a payout method and account to receive withdrawals, and are responsible for the accuracy of those details.</li>
                            <li>A withdrawal is a request. It is reviewed and processed by Brandora, and may be approved or rejected.</li>
                            <li>The withdrawal fee and the net payout amount are shown before a request is submitted.</li>
                        </ul>

                        <div class="tc-note">
                            <p>
                                Brandora does not guarantee that any individual transaction will
                                succeed, that a payment provider will be available, or that a
                                withdrawal will be processed within a particular time. Payments
                                depend on third-party providers and on the accuracy of the details
                                you supply.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <h3>Your responsibilities</h3>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Keep your payout details accurate. We are not responsible for funds sent to an account you entered incorrectly.</li>
                            <li>You are responsible for any taxes that apply to your earnings or expenditure. Brandora does not provide tax advice.</li>
                            <li>Do not arrange payment outside the platform in order to avoid platform fees (see section 11).</li>
                        </ul>

                    </article>


                    <!-- 9 -->

                    <article class="tc-card" id="messaging">

                        <h2>9. Messaging and Communication</h2>

                        <p>
                            Brands and influencers can message each other through the platform, either
                            generally or in the context of a particular campaign. Messages may include
                            text and attached media.
                        </p>

                        <ul>
                            <li>Keep communication professional and relevant to the collaboration.</li>
                            <li>Do not use messaging to harass, threaten, abuse, or spam another user.</li>
                            <li>Do not send unlawful, deceptive, or infringing material.</li>
                            <li>Do not use messaging to solicit users onto other platforms in order to bypass Brandora's payment and dispute mechanisms.</li>
                        </ul>

                        <p>
                            Messages exchanged in a collaboration may be reviewed by our team where it
                            is necessary to investigate a dispute or a report of misuse. Please treat
                            messaging as a business channel rather than a private one.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <!-- 10 -->

                    @* ASSUMPTION: ownership of campaign deliverables is not modelled anywhere
