                    <article class="tc-card" id="content-ip">

                        <h2>10. Content and Intellectual Property</h2>

                        <h3>Your content</h3>
                        <p>
                            You keep ownership of the content you upload &mdash; profile images,
                            campaign material, submitted deliverables, message attachments, and
                            anything else you provide. By uploading it, you grant Brandora a
                            non-exclusive licence to host, store, reproduce, and display that content
                            to the extent needed to operate the platform and provide the service to
                            you and to the users you are working with.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            You confirm that you own the content you upload or have the rights needed
                            to upload it, and that it does not infringe anyone else's rights.
                        </p>

                        <h3>Deliverables</h3>
                        <p>
                            Ownership of, and rights to use, the content an influencer produces for a
                            campaign are a matter for the agreement between the brand and the
                            influencer. Brandora does not assign those rights and takes no position on
                            them. We recommend that both sides agree in writing what the brand may do
                            with the content before work begins.
                        </p>

                        <h3>Uploads</h3>
                        <p>
                            Uploaded files are stored with our third-party media provider. The
                            platform accepts a defined set of image, video, and document formats and
                            enforces a maximum file size for each; files outside those limits will be
                            rejected. Do not attempt to upload executable content or disguise a file's
                            type.
                        </p>

                        <h3>Brandora's own material</h3>
                        <p>
                            The Brandora name, logo, interface, and the software behind the platform
                            belong to Brandora and may not be copied, reproduced, or used without our
                            written permission.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <!-- 11 -->

                    <article class="tc-card" id="prohibited">

                        <h2>11. Prohibited Activities</h2>

                        <p>
                            The following are not permitted on Brandora. This list is not exhaustive.
                        </p>

                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Misrepresentation:</strong> providing false identity, company, audience, or engagement information.</li>
                            <li><strong>Artificial engagement:</strong> using bought followers, bots, or any artificial means to inflate reach or engagement figures.</li>
                            <li><strong>Fee circumvention:</strong> moving an introduction made on Brandora off-platform in order to avoid platform fees or the milestone and dispute mechanisms.</li>
                            <li><strong>Abuse of other users:</strong> harassment, threats, discriminatory abuse, or spam.</li>
                            <li><strong>Unlawful or infringing content:</strong> uploading or commissioning content that is illegal, defamatory, obscene, or infringes someone else's rights.</li>
                            <li><strong>Deceptive advertising:</strong> publishing paid content without the disclosure required by law or by the relevant social platform.</li>
                            <li><strong>Platform abuse:</strong> scraping, automated data extraction, probing or testing the security of the service, or interfering with its normal operation.</li>
                            <li><strong>Account abuse:</strong> creating multiple or duplicate accounts to evade a restriction, manipulate verification, or misuse the dispute process.</li>
                            <li><strong>Fraud:</strong> chargeback abuse, fraudulent payment instruments, or any attempt to obtain funds you are not entitled to.</li>
                        </ul>

                        <p>
                            If you encounter any of the above, please report it to
                            <a href="mailto:care.brandora@gmail.com">care.brandora@gmail.com</a> or
                            through our <a href="/contact">contact form</a>.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <!-- 12 -->

                    @* ASSUMPTION: the Dispute model records a reason, a status, resolution
                       notes and a resolving admin, and held funds can be moved by an admin —
