                    <article class="tc-card" id="disputes">

                        <h2>12. Disputes and Resolution</h2>

                        <h3>Between users</h3>
                        <p>
                            Most disagreements are best settled directly. If a milestone is not what
                            was expected, the brand should request a revision and explain what is
                            wrong, and the influencer should have a fair opportunity to put it right.
                        </p>

                        <h3>Raising a dispute with Brandora</h3>
                        <p>
                            If that does not resolve matters, either party may raise a dispute against
                            a collaboration or a specific milestone, giving a reason. A dispute is
                            recorded, moves through review by our team, and is closed with resolution
                            notes.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            While a dispute is open, funds held for the affected milestone may remain
                            held until the dispute is closed. Where a resolution requires it, an
                            administrator may direct held funds to one party or the other, and that
                            action is recorded.
                        </p>

                        <div class="tc-note">
                            <p>
                                Our dispute process is an administrative service we provide to help
                                users reach a practical outcome. It is not arbitration, mediation, or
                                a legal determination of either party's rights, and we do not
                                guarantee any particular outcome, a refund, or a release of funds in
                                your favour.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                Nothing in this section prevents either party from pursuing its legal
                                rights independently of the platform.
                            </p>
                        </div>

                        <p>
                            Both parties are expected to engage with the process honestly and to
                            provide the information reasonably requested of them.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <!-- 13 -->

                    @* ASSUMPTION: the codebase has no defined handling for open collaborations
