                    <article class="tc-card" id="termination">

                        <h2>13. Account Suspension and Termination</h2>

                        <h3>By you</h3>
                        <p>
                            You may stop using Brandora at any time and ask us to close your account by
                            contacting support. Closing an account does not cancel obligations you have
                            already taken on, such as delivering work you have been paid for.
                        </p>

                        <h3>By Brandora</h3>
                        <p>
                            We may suspend or terminate an account, or restrict access to parts of the
                            platform, where we reasonably believe that:
                        </p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>these terms have been breached;</li>
                            <li>the information provided is false or misleading;</li>
                            <li>the account is being used fraudulently or unlawfully;</li>
                            <li>the account presents a risk to other users or to the platform; or</li>
                            <li>we are required to do so by law.</li>
                        </ul>

                        <p>
                            Where it is reasonable and lawful to do so, we will tell you why. Serious
                            cases &mdash; such as suspected fraud &mdash; may result in immediate
                            suspension without prior notice.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Open collaborations, milestones in progress, and any funds held at the time
                            of a suspension or termination will be dealt with in accordance with these
                            terms, including the dispute process in section 12. Termination does not
                            affect rights or liabilities that arose before it.
                        </p>

                    </article>


                    <!-- 14 -->

                    <article class="tc-card" id="availability">

                        <h2>14. Platform Availability and Third-Party Services</h2>

                        <p>
                            We work to keep Brandora available and working correctly, but we do not
                            promise uninterrupted or error-free service. Access may be interrupted by
                            maintenance, updates, technical faults, or events outside our control.
                        </p>

                        <p>
                            Parts of the platform depend on third parties, including:
                        </p>
                        <ul>
                            <li>a cloud media provider, which stores and delivers uploaded files;</li>
                            <li>mobile financial service providers, which process payments and payouts;</li>
                            <li>an email delivery service, which sends verification codes and notifications.</li>
